d the third is ``\site{rpf_e3}'': C$^*$ minus R3 at \const{0.03} is lower than without churn on only \site{rpf_d3_k} of six markets, so it fails the support criterion while meeting the material companion. Continued search moved both the no-churn baselines and the churn cells: the pooled C$^*$ minus R3 difference with the primary winners minus that with the all-frozen winners is \site{rp_sd0} without churn, \site{rp_sd3} at $p = \const{0.03}$, and \site{rp_sd5} at \const{0.05}. With the all-frozen winners the mean paired changes at \const{0.05} are \site{rpf_d5} ($d$), \site{rpf_q5} ($q$), and \site{rpf_u5} ($u$), further from zero than with the primary winners: at this rate the better-searched winner set gives the weaker changes. The paired changes therefore carry the search uncertainty of the baselines as well as that of the churn cells. As planned, the failed expectation is reported without a causal reading.
